From f74bf0309d86bf32029dd2ee18d55c25d77effc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: broken-branch <broken-branch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:10:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] usb: return errors, keep the endpoint, round and clamp
 digits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Find the display by enumerating and open that device, so the error
names the real cause: "not connected", or rusb's own "Access denied
(insufficient permissions)" or "Resource busy", instead of guessing.
Look up the interrupt OUT endpoint once at open time. Return errors
with context from claim() and send() rather than calling process::exit
inside the USB module; the caller decides. Treat a short write as an
error, since the panel checksums the frame.

Round temperatures to 0.1 °C and clamp them to the panel's 00.0-99.9
range. Previously 100 °C and above produced a digit of 10, and tenths
were truncated. Dashes for NaN and infinities. Add tests for both.
